1021..1099 Comment "/// Rotating by `b` and back is the identity (cubical\'s `rotInv-1`, `b · a ·"
1100..1180 Comment "/// invLooper b ≡ a`, `_·_` associating to the left). The obligation over `a`"
1181..1255 Comment "/// holds `b` at its point, where `mul(Base, a)` is `a` and the loop moves"
1256..1328 Comment "/// through `mul`\'s second argument as itself; the one over `b` moves it"
1329..1404 Comment "/// through both of the outer `mul`\'s arguments, the loop then its inverse."
1405..1481 Comment "/// The square of the two loops is not owed: the paths of the circle are its"
1482..1499 Comment "/// words, a set."
